# CODEX.md example

Defaults for Codex-style workflow:
- if you cannot read external links, ask for the markdown files directly
- work from `git diff`
- do not run destructive commands without approval
- report what changed, what was checked and what still needs follow-up

## Codex token-aware discovery

When code discovery is needed, keep the main process focused on decisions and implementation.

If available, delegate broad repository search to a cheaper or faster read-only subagent such as Codex Spark.

The subagent must return:
- `path:line`
- symbol / component / route
- relevant snippet or signature
- why it matters
- confidence

The main process should use that map for targeted reading and implementation, verifying critical findings before editing.

Possible routing:
- Spark or another cheaper read-only subagent for broad discovery;
- the main model for decisions and implementation;
- a separate reviewer for independent diff review.
